// SecondaryResults - tabs
"view.secondaryresults.help"                     = "The information shown in this screen depends on your configuration. This includes both the choice of factors in the radix and the factors you want to use for secondary directions.\n\nYou see four tabs.\n\nThe 'Positions' tab shows an overview of the secondary positions, both in longitude and declination.\n\nThe 'Midpoints' tab shows an overview of both the directed planet relative to midpoints in the radix, and an overview of directed midpoints where a radix planet is located.\n\nThe 'Matches' tab shows which secondary directions form an aspect with a point in the radix. You also see the orb and the exactness of the aspect.\n\nThe 'Dual Wheel' tab shows the horoscope with the secondary positions in an extra ring. Above the chart you see three icons to switch between color and black-and-white, turn aspects on and off, and export the chart to a PNG file.";
"view.secondaryresults.title"                    = "Secondary Direction Positions";
"view.secondaryresults.noresults"                = "Select an event and press Calculate to see positions.";
